<section class="philosophy" id="philosophy" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
  <div class="philosophy__container section-reveal">
    <h2 class="philosophy__title" id="philosophy-heading">An Act of Faith</h2>
    <div class="philosophy__content">
      <p class="philosophy__text">
        Only one in four software engineers is happy in their current role. The rest are burning
        out — buried in maintenance, context-switching, and systems that were designed to extract
        output, not to cultivate craft.
      </p>
      <p class="philosophy__text">
        <strong>Paradius</strong> was born from a simple conviction: the quality of what we build can
        never be separated from how we treat the people who build it. When engineers work where their
        craft is respected — where architecture comes first and shortcuts are not negotiable —
        something shifts. They stop performing. They start creating.
      </p>
      <p class="philosophy__text">
        At Paradius, we filter carefully. We collaborate, never delegate. And we build from the
        foundation up, because what is laid right does not need to be rebuilt.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="philosophy__quote">
        <p>
          For engineers: a place where you spend your time building, not fighting the system. For
          companies: software built by people who chose to be here — and it shows in every line.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
